{"conversation":"Okay, so I think there must be exactly two "S" in each section. Maybe I can find all the 'S' in the corridor and then count the spaces between them to put dividers? The plants don't really affect the count, but the positions between seats do. Maybe if I find positions between pairs of 'S', those would be possible divider spots. So I should probably identify positions between every 2nd 'S', then count how many 'P's are between those. If there are some 'P's, I can maybe put dividers in those gaps in several ways.","python_code":"class Solution:
